 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved now\nFrom his former burdens, and pacified,\nAs though with joy he smote those happy thousand,\nWhich had been his home for so many multiplied.\nBut last in all these scenes came this another\nSword, which was the first that I've never\nSeen of any truth on such form rather,\nBut as it seemed to me did look terribly\nLike one who could not be. Indeed, indeed,\nThe length was not quite the same, nor again\nThe face, but I'll gladly confess even\nThat there is no more wanton disdain",
